<title>SRI LANKA: Airlanka wants six flights to UK a week-paper.</title>
<headline>Airlanka wants six flights to UK a week-paper.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>British and Sri Lankan aviation officials will meet in London on July 29-30 to discuss increasing Airlanka's weekly flights to Britain, the state-run Daily News said on Friday.</p>
<p>The newspaper quoted aviation sources as saying the national carrier, which now operates four direct A340 flights per week from Colombo to London, wanted two more flights.</p>
<p>It said Airlanka needed two extra flights to relieve congestion on a route popular with business travellers and to cater to increased tourist traffic.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
